{"delayMs":2,"event":{"seq":3,"runId":"run_20511753ab79","ts":"2026-07-14T17:58:53.122Z","type":"run.plan_generated","payload":{"plan":[{"index":0,"title":"Inspect existing repo files","detail":"Read Makefile and main.c to understand the build system, existing scaffolding, RTT integration points, and any already-present peripheral init. This informs what must be written from scratch vs. what can be extended.","riskLevel":"low","hardwareAction":false},{"index":1,"title":"Write BMP180 I2C firmware from scratch into main.c","detail":"Implement register-level I2C1 driver for STM32F303RE (8 MHz HSI, TIMINGR=0x10420F13 for ~100 kHz standard-mode). Steps: RCC enable GPIOB + I2C1, configure PB8/PB9 as AF4 open-drain, initialise I2C1, read chip-ID (0xD0 \u2192 expect 0x55), read 22-byte calibration block (0xAA\u20130xBF), trigger UT and UP measurements (OSS=3), compute temperature and pressure using BMP180 datasheet compensation algorithm, print results via RTT (SEGGER_RTT_printf). Include an infinite loop that samples at ~1 Hz.","riskLevel":"low","hardwareAction":false},{"index":2,"title":"Build firmware","detail":"Run 'make clean && make' via build_firmware. Check exit code is 0 and rtt-f303re.elf is produced. Fix any compile errors (within iteration budget) before proceeding.","riskLevel":"low","hardwareAction":false},{"index":3,"title":"Flash firmware to Nucleo-F303RE","detail":"Flash rtt-f303re.elf using pyocd (approval-gated). Verify probe is reachable via list_targets before flashing.","riskLevel":"medium","hardwareAction":true},{"index":4,"title":"Capture I2C traffic with logic analyzer","detail":"Run capture_during with I2C protocol decode (CH0=SDA, CH1=SCL, ~100 kHz) for ~5 seconds while the firmware is running. Verify: SCL frequency in [90 kHz, 110 kHz], device ACK at address 0x77, chip-ID byte 0x55 present in decoded frames.","riskLevel":"low","hardwareAction":true},{"index":5,"title":"Read RTT log and verify sensor output","detail":"Use read_firmware_log (RTT) to capture ~10 seconds of output. Verify chip-ID line matches 0x55, temperature is in plausible range [10, 50] \u00b0C (\u00d70.1 units: 100\u2013500), pressure is in plausible range [85000, 110000] Pa.","riskLevel":"low","hardwareAction":true},{"index":6,"title":"Record all checks and write final report","detail":"Call record_check for every registered check, then write_report with full evidence linking (artifact IDs, sourceRef to BMP180 datasheet sections). If any check fails, call declare_diagnosis before attempting a fix iteration.","riskLevel":"low","hardwareAction":false}],"riskSummary":"Two hardware mutations occur: (1) flash_firmware writes new code to the Nucleo-F303RE's flash \u2014 this is approval-gated by the harness and will not proceed without explicit human sign-off; (2) the logic analyzer capture activates the Kingst LA2016 to sniff the I2C bus passively (read-only, no board power interaction). The flash operation carries medium risk: if the firmware has a hard fault the board will reset-loop, but the ST-LINK allows recovery by reflashing. No erase-only operations are planned. All other steps (file edits, builds, RTT reads) are purely software and carry no hardware risk."}}}
